    "text": "STAT GR 5293 Sec002 | Spring 2026\nConcrete example using base Transformer as reference\n●Use the base Transformer model presented by Vaswani et al. 2017:\n○Transformer weights have dimensions 𝑑× 𝑘= 512 × 64\n○So 512 × 64 = 32,768 trainable parameters\nIn LoRA with rank 𝑟= 8:\n●𝐴 has dimensions 𝑟× 𝑘= 8 × 64 = 512 parameters\n●𝐵 has dimensions 𝑑× 𝑟= 512 × 8 = 4,096 parameters\n●86% reduction in parameters to train!\n512\n64\n512\n64\n8",
    "method": "native",
